# Defining AI

#### We'll dive into more of the vocabulary around AI in the next module, but here's a quick introduction to some key terms.

<div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Artificial Intelligence (AI):</strong> A broad term for computer systems designed to perform tasks that usually require human thinking, such as recognizing patterns, making decisions, or understanding language.</p>
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Generative AI:</strong> A type of AI that can create new content, like text, images, video, audio, or computer code.</p>
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Large Language Models (LLMs):</strong> Very large computer programs trained on huge amounts of text. They are especially good at understanding questions and generating human-like written responses.</p>
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>AI Chatbots:</strong> The conversational tools (the chat interface) that people use to interact with AI models, usually by typing or speaking.</p>
</div>

#### You may be familiar with one or more of the following AI tools:

<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;width:95%;margin:20pt auto;padding:0 5px;">
<div style="width:20%;text-align:center;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/c22ec02e808ca32157566d9fb91efbe0-Screenshot%202026-01-29%20at%2011.40.54%20AM.png" alt="ChatGPT Logo" style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto !important;max-height:90px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:5pt;margin:0 auto;">
